     [0;90;1m│[0m [0;96mNote: A written Show drifts as the type changes, and a Read written to match it drifts separately, so the pair stops roundtripping while it still compiles. Deriving keeps both in step with the fields. An instance that ignores the value prints the same text whatever it is handed, which is how a secret stays out of the logs.[0m
